  "body": "Found while reviewing PR 1622 (the stock-source law of issue 1607). Read from the code and the PR body; not reproduced by a run yet.\n\nWhat happens: PR 1622 gives a 2D operation whose source is the stock a part law for the pocket family, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Circular, Contour, Face, Engrave and Trace (`keep_law::is_stock_kept_kind`). 2D Chamfer and the hole kinds (Drill, Bore, Thread) on a stock source stay at `DepthLaw::None`; the PR body says so under \"not exercised\" (\"not in #1607's list; the chamfer's depth is derived and its break is credited only on the part, the hole kinds would need modelled hole rims excused\"). Such an operation that cuts into a part standing in the stock has no operation finding. On an aligned stock the program simulation can still hold it; on a turned stock the simulation refuses to judge, so the program posts.\n\nExpected: a cut into a held part is a blocking finding on the operation whatever its kind, or the post is refused by name where no law can judge it (Prime Directive: correct, or visibly refused).\n\nEvidence: `crates/app/src/operation/keep_law.rs` (`is_stock_kept_kind`, `parts_in_stock`), `depth_law_of`, `run_job` in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` at PR 1622 head c74d888d; the same holds on main, where no stock-source kind outside the pocket family is judged.\n\nOpen design points: what a chamfer's break may remove on a stock source; how a drilled or bored hole's own rim in the part is excused without excusing a hole through a neighbouring part.\n\nDone means: a test per kind (Chamfer, Drill, Bore, Thread) with a stock source and a part in the cut, on an aligned and on a turned stock, shows a blocking finding or a named post refusal; a legal case of each kind still posts.\n",
